From: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: accept any MY_MAC entry on
 ingress

Each port ingress L3 interface selected only its own MY_MAC entry, so a
frame addressed to any other address of this router fell through to L2
forwarding by the FDB and never reached software. On a board whose
ports sit under a software bridge that happens for the bridge address
whenever the frame arrives on a different member.

Accept all MY_MAC entries: every one is by construction an address of
this router, so routing such frames to the CPU is always correct. The
qca-ssdk accumulates the same bitmap per interface and its bridge
manager adds group addresses to every member.

Reproducer and measurement on TP-Link Archer BE800 (IPQ9574, lan1
cabled to lan4, lan4 in a network namespace): before, a namespace peer
saw 100 percent RX loss and unreachable routes; after, ping 0.2 ms and
NAT hardware offload unchanged at 2.35 Gbit/s.

Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c	2026-10-02 08:00:46.540002523 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c	2026-10-02 08:00:46.560002523 +0000
@@ -798,7 +798,7 @@
 	in.mtu = mtu;
 	in.mru_ipv6 = mtu;
 	in.mtu_ipv6 = mtu;
-	in.mac_bitmap = BIT(my_mac);
+	in.mac_bitmap = GENMASK(PPE_MY_MAC_TBL_ENTRIES - 1, 0);
 	in.ipv4_uc_route_en = true;
 	in.ipv6_uc_route_en = true;
 	/* Hardware decrements the TTL, so an expired one must come back
